title: November 2022

@november_2022_hub
# prose-audit: Grade A — Przewodów now has the grain dryer, the half-past-three, the two farm workers and the evening on which the anonymous briefings moved; verify, attribute and blame each end somewhere with a cost. The Independence sub-event states what the accumulated work means instead of counting it.
title: Independence Day and a missile
face-image: img/poland/events/independence-march-2021.webp
new-page: true

= November 2022

Our annual contest over Independence Day is followed by a lethal explosion
near the Ukrainian border. The first asks what we have built in the street;
the second asks whether we can resist speaking before the evidence arrives.

- @nov22_independence
- @nov22_przewodow
- @nov22_konf
- @nov22_finish

@nov22_independence
title: The Independence Day March
new-page: true
view-if: independence_2022_done = 0
on-arrival: independence_2022_done = 1; independence_march_2022_done = 1; last_independence_march_year = 2022; far_right_street_capacity += 2; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -5; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 6

= The annual test under wartime pressure

The war has changed the slogans and settled nothing about who may speak for the
nation. Most of the march will carry Ukrainian flags beside Polish ones. A
minority will carry placards about refugees and benefits, and the organisers
have made no arrangement to stop them.

[? if civic_independence_years > 0: Our own commemoration is now something
people expect. A tradition survives by being repeated; drop it this year and
the volunteers who built it will find another use for their November.?]
[? if independence_monitor_years > 0: The observers have done this before and
are better at it than they were. They will be on the route unless somebody
stands them down.?]
[? if independence_join_years > 0: The social-patriotic current has marched
inside the procession before and wants to again. Under wartime conditions that
means standing near the anti-Ukrainian placards and answering for them, rather
than explaining afterwards that they were nothing to do with us.?]

- @nov22_civic
- @nov22_join
- @nov22_counter
- @nov22_monitor
- @nov22_ukraine

@nov22_civic
title: Make civic independence an annual Left institution
subtitle: [? if civic_independence_investment >= 3: The civic network now funds the annual event itself. No resource cost.?][? if civic_independence_investment < 3: Cost: 1 resource.?]
choose-if: civic_independence_investment >= 3 or resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The annual event lacks support.
on-arrival: resources -= 1 if civic_independence_investment < 3; civic_independence_investment += 1 if civic_independence_investment < 3; independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition"; civic_independence_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 5; local_network += 2; public_trust += 2; labor_credibility += 2; far_right_agenda -= 1; news_headline = "The Left returns to Independence Day with its own tradition"

Trade union banners, municipal organisers and the civic-independence network
return under a banner they now expect to raise every November. Repetition turns
the commemoration into an institution rather than a one-year reply to the
nationalist march.

- @nov22_return: Return to the November desk

